{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note-header",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 1620
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Sinnamary S1+S2 Fusion — Phase 2",
        "params": {
          "text": "# Sinnamary S1+S2 Fusion — Phase 2\n\n**Goal:** Enrich the Phase 1 SAR-only baseline with Sentinel-2 spectral indices for better mangrove / orpaillage discrimination.\n\n**Why S2?** S1 alone confuses mangrove (double-bounce) with flooded non-mangrove wetlands, and bare orpaillage soil with natural river bars. S2 MNDWI + EVI break these ambiguities.\n\n## Pipeline\n🟦 **S1 branch (left):** S1 RTC 2024 → s1_polarization_features (6 radar indices)\n🟩 **S2 branch (centre):** S2 L2A 2024 → 3 × spectral_index (NDVI, MNDWI, EVI) → stacked via geo_band_stack\n🟧 **Fusion (right):** geo_band_stack merges S1 + S2 stacks → 9-band feature raster\n🟥 **LULC change (bottom):** geo_time_align 2017→2024 + ESA WorldCover ground truth\n\n## Expected enrichment vs Phase 1\n- Mangrove vs dry forest F1: +8–15 % (NDVI NIR discriminates)\n- Orpaillage false positives: ÷3 (MNDWI + EVI vs natural bare soil)\n- Turbidity proxy: MNDWI aval directly comparable to Naïades stations",
          "width": 1560,
          "height": 280,
          "fontSize": 13,
          "color_index": 4
        }
      },
      "width": 1133,
      "height": 378,
      "selected": false,
      "positionAbsolute": {
        "x": 640,
        "y": 1620
      },
      "dragging": false
    },
